DEVIATIONS
----------
Changes made in Hanzo Node relative to the upstream Shinkai Node:

- Rebranded the crate and directory layout from shinkai-* to hanzo-*: the base
  import shipped shinkai-bin/, shinkai-libs/, shinkai-test-framework/, and
  shinkai-test-macro/; this tree ships hanzo-bin/ (hanzo-node, hanzoai),
  hanzo-libs/, hanzo-test-framework/, and hanzo-test-macro/.
- Added a Go integration layer (go.mod module github.com/hanzoai/node) whose
  main.go and node.go construct a github.com/luxfi/node application and register
  the cevm (C-Chain), dexvm (D-Chain), and thresholdvm (T-Chain) virtual
  machines; the upstream is Rust-only.
- Added post-quantum cryptography under hanzo-libs/hanzo-pqc (with
  pqc_benchmarks) and the hanzo-brain library under hanzo-libs/hanzo-brain.
- Repointed container images to the Hanzo registry: compose.yml pulls
  ghcr.io/hanzoai/node and ghcr.io/hanzoai/engine.
- Moved CI to self-hosted Actions Runner Controller scale sets
  (hanzo-build-linux-amd64 / hanzo-build-linux-arm64) instead of GitHub-hosted
  runners, per .github/workflows/build-binaries.yml and cicd.yml.
- Rebranded product surfaces in README.md to "Hanzo Node", pointing at
  docs.hanzo.ai and the hanzoai/hanzo-apps companion repository.
- Publishes the node libraries to crates.io under hanzo-* names (for example
  hanzo-mcp 1.1.21), replacing the upstream shinkai-* crate names.
- Slimmed the Cargo workspace: members are reduced to the shipped binaries plus
  their test crates, with the broader hanzo-libs cluster consumed from crates.io
  via the standalone hanzonet workspace (see the [workspace] comment in
  Cargo.toml), versus the upstream monorepo's larger set of path members.
- Added Hanzo-specific documentation under docs/, including
  docs/COMPUTE_BROKER.md.
- Unified the workspace version line at 1.1.x with authorship
  "Nico Arqueros <nico@hanzo.ai>" in Cargo.toml.
